    (property "Description" "ESP32 DevKit V1, 30-pin (2x15) board (aka \"DOIT ESP32 DevKit V1\"). STRAPPING PINS: never drive/pull GPIO12 HIGH before boot completes (flash voltage select, causes bootloop) - avoid it for signals a peripheral could hold high, e.g. generic SPI MISO. GPIO15 LOW at boot only suppresses the UART boot log (cosmetic). GPIO2 must float/LOW at boot. Full rationale: libraries/docs/mcu/ESP32-DevKitV1.md" (id 4) (at 0.0 0.0 0)
